{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.StandardModel.LeptonNumberCarrierChirality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.StandardModel.LeptonNumberCarrierChirality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Function.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.chiral_carrier_admits_lepton_number","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.chiral_carrier_admits_lepton_number","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberCarrierChirality.lean#L138-L149","doc":"**The obstruction is exactly amphichirality — nothing more.**\n\nAs soon as the mirror moves the carrier, a lepton-number function with the\nrequired values exists.  So chirality of the carrier is *sufficient* as well\nas necessary, and the negative above is sharp: it rules out the unknot, not\nthe idea. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.mirror_must_move_the_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.mirror_must_move_the_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberCarrierChirality.lean#L126-L136","doc":"**The actionable form: the carrier must be chiral.**\n\nAny `L` that separates a particle from its antiparticle by mirroring forces\nthe carrier to be moved by the mirror.  The unknot is not such a carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.no_lepton_number_on_amphichiral_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.no_lepton_number_on_amphichiral_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/StandardModel/LeptonNumberCarrierChirality.lean#L108-L124","doc":"**The obstruction.**\n\nIf the mirror involution fixes a carrier `x`, no `ℤ`-valued function of the\ncarrier can assign `+1` to the particle and `-1` to its mirror image.\n\nApplied to a carrier the mirror fixes — e.g. the unknot read as a bare knot\ntype — this shows `L` cannot be a function of that carrier alone.  It is not\na statement about the corpus table, whose carriers are braid-level; see the\nmodule docstring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}